          "description": "Location: Karachi (Onsite)\nEmployment Type: Full-Time\nAbout the Role\nTech Inoviq Solutions is looking for a talented Software Engineer to join our team in Karachi. This is an exciting opportunity to work dedicatedly with an Australian HealthTech company developing innovative software used in clinical healthcare environments.\nYou will be part of an international engineering team, building new features, solving technical challenges, and contributing to a modern web application used by healthcare professionals.\nResponsibilities\nDevelop and maintain applications using React (TypeScript) and NestJS (Node.js).\nBuild new features and enhance existing functionality.\nTroubleshoot and resolve software issues efficiently.\nWrite clean, maintainable, and well-tested code.\nCollaborate with an international development team.\nParticipate in code reviews and follow engineering best practices.\nEnsure application quality through testing and debugging.\nRequirements\nStrong experience with React.js and TypeScript.\nExperience with NestJS or other Node.js backend frameworks.\nGood understanding of REST APIs.\nFamiliarity with Git and modern development workflows.\nStrong debugging and problem-solving skills.\nAbility to work independently and take ownership of tasks.\nDemonstrated competence using Claude Code (or similar agentic AI coding tools) in real development work.\nComfortable working with some overlap with Australian business hours.\nNice to Have\nPostgreSQL\nDocker\nMicrosoft Azure\nHealthcare or medical software experience (DICOM, HL7)\nExperience with AI coding tools such as Claude Code, GitHub Copilot, or Cursor\nWhat we Offer\nOpportunity to work on an international product.\nExposure to Australian clients and engineering practices.\nCompetitive salary.\nCareer growth and learning opportunities.\nCollaborative and professional work environment.\nLong-term employment with Tech Inoviq Solutions.\nApply by sending your CV to: hr@techinoviq.com with subject line Software Engineer - HealthTech",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4475049119": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-18T01:02:47.116527+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About FullStack\nFullStack is your AI-native engineering partner, built to turn AI capability into certainty. Most companies can demo AI; few can get it to production and prove what it produced. We close that gap with three capabilities, AI built into your products from the start, elite vetted talent who apply it, and transparent execution that shows value every step of the way. With now over 600 customers in North America, FullStack is one integrated partner for all your AI engineering needs. With FullStack, you move forward with confidence.\nWe’re Most Proud Of\nOffering life-changing career opportunities to talented software professionals across the Americas.\nBuilding highly-skilled software development teams for hundreds of the world’s greatest companies.\nHaving delivered hundreds of successful custom software solutions, which have positively impacted the lives and careers of millions of users.\nOur 4.1-star rating on GlassDoor.\nOur client Net Promoter Score of 68, twice the industry average.\nThe Opportunity\nJoin our talent network and connect with U.S. clients for flexible, project-based development work as an Agentic Software Engineer (Google Antigravity).\nYou will integrate directly into our client's team and work alongside their existing designers and engineers on a daily basis.\nWhat We're Looking For\n5+ years of professional software development experience with a deep understanding of full-stack architectures (e.g., Java, Python, C#, React, Node, etc.).\n1-3 years of professional experience using Google Antigravity as a primary development environment to coordinate AI-driven implementation across large, multi-file systems while maintaining architectural oversight.\nExperience delivering production software where AI systems generate the majority of implementation code.\nStrong context engineering skills, including structuring codebases, specifications, and documentation to produce reliable, context-efficient AI output.\nAbility to translate complex product requirements into machine-executable, AI-friendly specifications.\nExperience designing AI-first development workflows from specification through deployment.\nAbility to systematically improve AI-generated output through structured iteration and feedback loops.\nComfort working across multiple stacks, using AI to deliver high-quality, production-ready systems.\nExperience operating across frontend, backend, and infrastructure in AI-accelerated environments.\nDisciplined human-in-the-loop review practices, with risk-adjusted validation for high-impact or safety-critical flows.\nStrong curiosity and initiative in evaluating and adopting emerging AI-native engineering practices.\nAdvanced understanding of Agile methodologies and Lean principles and participation in team ceremonies as well as asynchronous work.\nAdvanced English is required.\nSuccessful completion of a four-year college degree is required.\nA positive mindset and a can-do attitude.\nAbility to identify with the goals of FullStack's clients and dedicate yourself to delivering on commitments.\nAbility to consistently work 40 hours per week.\nWork Authorization Requirements\nApplicants must be currently authorized to work in the country of this job posting on a full-time basis.\nFullStack will not sponsor applicants for work visas now or in the future.\nWhat We Offer\nCompetitive pay.\n100% remote work.\nThe ability to work with leading startups and Fortune 500 companies.\nContinuing education opportunities.\nOpportunity to grow and expand your career.\nOur talent network is committed to fostering a diverse, inclusive, and accessible environment where IT professionals can find opportunities that match their skills. We welcome individuals of all races, religions, genders, sexual orientations, national origins, abilities, and experiences. Our focus is on connecting talent with projects based on qualifications, ensuring a fair and transparent process that values diverse perspectives and global collaboration.\nLearn more about our Applicants Privacy Notice.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4475539733": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-18T01:02:47.116527+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "As an hourly paid, fully remote Rust Engineer for AI Data Training, you will review AI-generated Rust code and explanations or generate your own, evaluate the reasoning quality and step-by-step problem-solving, and provide expert feedback that helps models produce answers that are accurate, logical, and clearly explained. You will assess solutions for correctness, safety, and adherence to the prompt; identify errors in ownership, borrowing, lifetimes, or algorithmic reasoning; fact-check information; write high-quality explanations and model solutions that demonstrate idiomatic Rust patterns; and rate and compare multiple AI responses based on correctness and reasoning quality. This role is with SME Careers, a fast-growing AI Data Services company and subsidiary of SuperAnnotate that provides AI training data for many of the world’s largest AI companies and foundation model labs. Your work will directly help improve the world’s premier AI models while giving you the flexibility of impactful, detail-oriented remote contract work.\nImportant\nThere is no immediate project for this role; however, if qualified, you will be among the first experts we reach out to when relevant opportunities arise. This will also provide you with access to future projects available through our expert network.\nKey Responsibilities\nDevelop AI Training Content: Create detailed prompts in various topics and responses to guide AI learning, ensuring the models reflect a comprehensive understanding of diverse subjects.\nOptimize AI Performance: Evaluate and rank AI responses to enhance the model's accuracy, fluency, and contextual relevance.\nEnsure Model Integrity: Test AI models for potential inaccuracies or biases, validating their reliability across use cases.\nYour Profile\n1–2+ years of professional Rust development experience in backend, CLI, or systems-focused projects.\nStrong understanding of Rust’s ownership, borrowing, and lifetime model, with the ability to reason clearly about aliasing and data races.\nSolid software engineering experience in at least one of backend services, command-line tools, or systems programming using Rust.\nAbility to evaluate safe, idiomatic Rust code, including appropriate use of traits, generics, pattern matching, and error handling.\nSignificant experience using LLMs or AI coding assistants while programming, combined with a disciplined approach to validating their output.\nExcellent English writing skills, capable of producing precise, structured, and pedagogical technical explanations.\nMinimum Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science or a closely related technical field.\nPrevious experience with AI data training, code review at scale, or evaluation of AI-generated technical content is strongly preferred; Minimum C1 English proficiency and an extremely detail-oriented working style are required.\nHighly preferred: experience with Tokio, Actix, Serde, and async Rust patterns in production or advanced side projects.\nPreferred: competitive programming experience, contributions to Rust open-source ecosystems, and demonstrated ability to reason about performance, concurrency, and correctness in Rust code.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4482142772": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-18T01:02:47.116527+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Job Description\nDoes the opportunity to develop and produce high performance systems excite you?\nDo you thrive when given the freedom to innovate?\nJoin our world-class Edge Technology organization\nThe Edge Platform team plans, builds, maintains, and operates a global platform, ensuring reliable availability and performance for customers. It designs, develops, and deploys essential technologies, including hardware, software, and network infrastructure, supporting all products.\nPartner with the best\nAs a Software Engineer I, you'll work on high-reliability/high-throughput systems that manage our customer's security certificates and configurations. Our team provides support to several other teams at Akamai who require secure delivery. Our work centers around building systems which operate at large scale, with high resilience and performance.\nAs a Software Engineer I, you will be responsible for:\nDesigning and developing systems capable of handling tens of thousands of concurrent operations\nDeveloping software to make efficient use of Relational Database Management Systems and NoSQL databases\nCreating new features from scratch, enhancing existing features and optimizing existing functionality\nFollowing good development methodology, including collaboration with testing and SQA departments to successfully deploy new system components\nDo What You Love\nTo be successful in this role you will:\nHave a Bachelor's degree in Computer Science or a related field\nPossess academic or project-based training in Java and familiarity with Python, C++, or Bash in Linux/Unix environments\nHave hands-on project experience with Spring and Spring Boot frameworks for building scalable backend applications\nHave hands-on project experience with UI technologies through academic or practical project experience using Angular for front-end development solutions.\nDemonstrate foundational understanding or project coursework in Terraform.\nDemonstrate understanding of SQL, relational databases (e.g., Oracle, SQL Server, MySQL, Postgres), and NoSQL databases (e.g., Elasticsearch, Cassandra) through projects.\nAbout Us\nAt Akamai, we make life better for billions of people, trillions of times a day.\nWhether you're streaming live events, scrolling social media, watching your favorite series, or managing your savings, we're the engine behind the scenes. We provide the world's most distributed platform from Cloud to Edge to help the giants of the digital world work faster and stay more secure, making the internet a better experience for everyone.\nOur Focus Is Simple\nCloud and Edge: Running apps closer to users for instant performance.\nSecurity : Neutralizing threats before they ever reach your data.\nContent Delivery : Scaling the world's biggest moments without a glitch.\nAI : Enabling our customers to build, secure, and scale AI apps on the world's most distributed cloud platform.\nAt Akamai, we don't just support the internet; we power and protect it, because behind every great digital experience is a massive hidden challenge. And we're the ones who solve it. When millions of people hit play or pay, Akamai ensures it just works.\nBenefits at Akamai: We support your health, well-being, finances, and life beyond work. See our benefits.\nFlexBase adapts to your job's needs\nAkamai's FlexBase program is yet another way we show our commitment to providing employees with an exceptional workplace experience. It's not about telling employees where to work; it's about supporting employees to do their best work.\nWe trust our incredible employees to work in ways that suit them best: at home, in an office, or a combination of both.\nConnect with us on social and see what life at Akamai is like!\nCompensation\nAkamai is committed to fair and equitable compensation practices. For US based candidates only - the base salary for this position ranges from $75,700 - $136,300/year; a candidate’s salary is determined by various factors including, but not limited to, relevant work experience, skills, certifications and location. Compensation for candidates outside the US will vary. The compensation package may also include incentive compensation opportunities in the form of annual bonus or incentives, equity awards and an Employee Stock Purchase Plan (ESPP). Akamai provides industry-leading benefits including healthcare, 401K savings plan, company holidays, vacation (in the form of PTO), sick time, family friendly benefits including parental leave and an employee assistance program including a focus on mental and financial wellness; Eligibility requirements apply.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4482170870": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-18T01:02:47.116527+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About FullStack\nFullStack is your AI-native engineering partner, built to turn AI capability into certainty. Most companies can demo AI; few can get it to production and prove what it produced. We close that gap with three capabilities, AI built into your products from the start, elite vetted talent who apply it, and transparent execution that shows value every step of the way. With now over 600 customers in North America, FullStack is one integrated partner for all your AI engineering needs. With FullStack, you move forward with confidence.\nWe’re Most Proud Of\nOffering life-changing career opportunities to talented software professionals across the Americas.\nBuilding highly-skilled software development teams for hundreds of the world’s greatest companies.\nHaving delivered hundreds of successful custom software solutions, which have positively impacted the lives and careers of millions of users.\nOur 4.1-star rating on GlassDoor.\nOur client Net Promoter Score of 68, twice the industry average.\nThe Position\nForward Deployed Engineers sit inside the client’s problem, not next to it. You embed with an enterprise team, find the work that actually warrants AI, architect the system, build it, and make it hold up in the real environment.\nThis is a three-way role: consultant, operator, engineer . You should be as comfortable pressure-testing a business case with a COO or VP of Engineering as you are debugging why an agent’s tool-calling loop degraded after a context change. The people who succeed here can hold a discovery conversation on Monday and ship what they scoped on Thursday.\nOn this track, your edge is application engineering: you make agents real inside the client’s actual systems, workflows, and delivery pipelines.\nWe work with regulated industries and Fortune 500 clients who have AI mandates, real constraints, and low tolerance for demos that don’t hold up.\nHow We Approach The Work\nFDEs are trusted to shape the solution, not only deliver it. Every engagement calls for architect-level judgment:\nReframes the request. Treats “we need an agent for X” as a hypothesis, not a spec.\nDecomposes the problem. Outcome → process → decisions → data → systems → actors → constraints — before choosing technology.\nChooses the intervention. Remove, simplify, traditional software, automation, LLM, RAG, agent, or multi-agent — and defends why.\nOwns the architecture decision. Documents trade-offs (ADRs), sets success metrics, pushes back on scope that won’t deliver value.\nConsultative Discovery\nClients rarely arrive with a fully formed problem, and the FDE’s first contribution is helping them see it clearly. You lead discovery with genuine curiosity, moving the conversation from stated requirements to underlying needs, and you build credibility through the depth of your understanding rather than the breadth of your pitch.\nUncovers business drivers. What outcome matters, what it’s worth, why now, and what happens if nothing changes.\nUncovers personal drivers. What each stakeholder is measured on, what they’re worried about, and what a win looks like for them individually.\nSurfaces constraints early. Security, compliance, data access, budget, skills, politics, timelines — the things that kill projects in month two.\nAligns stakeholders. Spots conflicting goals between business, engineering, and risk, and brings them to a shared definition of success.\nAsks strategic questions. Follows the answer with “why,” “how do you know,” and “what happens today when…” — without interrogating. Clients leave the conversation understanding their own problem better.\nEarns authority through depth. Credibility comes from the quality of the questions and the insight in the playback, not from pitching technology.\nWhat You'll Do\nDiscover. Run workshops and process discovery with business and engineering stakeholders. Separate genuine AI problems from workflow problems wearing an AI costume. Come back with a scoped, defensible point of view.\nStructure the process and the spec. For any business or engineering process being automated, map the current state, decision points, and exceptions, then turn it into specifications that both people and AI systems can execute against reliably.\nArchitect & design. Design agentic systems end to end — orchestration, context and retrieval architecture, tool and MCP integration, guardrails, human-in-the-loop checkpoints, and the boundaries between deterministic and non-deterministic components.\nBuild. Ship working systems — agents, multi-step automations, internal tooling, integration layers. You are hands-on. Prototypes that prove value in weeks, not slideware.\nEngineer the delivery system. Own CI/CD for what you build: build, test, release, environments.\nConsult. Present to and defend decisions in front of CTOs, VPs of Engineering, and business leadership. Quantify impact in their terms. Support pre-sales scoping and proposal work when the deal calls for it.\nWhat We're Looking For\n5+ years of professional software development experience with at least one mainstream production stack (TypeScript/Node.js, Python, Java, C#/.NET, or Go).\n1 - 4 years of professional experience building and shipping LLM-powered and agentic AI systems beyond prototypes or demos.\nAdvanced English is required.\nSuccessful completion of a four-year college degree is required.\nHands-on experience with frontier AI developer tools including Cursor, Claude Code, Gemini CLI, or OpenAI Codex.\nProven experience evaluating current-state environments and defining technical roadmaps.\nDemonstrated experience with APIs, service design, event-driven and distributed systems, and data modeling.\nExperience designing and owning CI/CD pipelines, including build, test, release, environments, and deployment processes.\nStrong understanding of context and specification engineering to produce reliable AI output.\nSolid understanding of enterprise integration patterns, including APIs, webhooks, event streams, iPaaS platforms such as n8n or MuleSoft, and MCP.\nTrack record of leading client-facing discovery calls, asking \"why\" before \"how\" to decompose unstructured business problems.\nSkilled at exercising end-to-end delivery ownership and managing project scope without requiring product manager supervision.\nAbility to work through new and difficult issues and contribute to libraries as needed.\nAbility to create and maintain continuous integration and delivery of applications.\nForensic attention to detail.\nA positive mindset and a can-do attitude.\nExperience working on Agile / Scrum teams.\nMeaningful experience working on large, complex systems.\nAbility to take extreme ownership over your work. Every day is a challenge to ensure you are performing to the expectations you and your team have agreed upon.\nAbility to identify with the goals of FullStack's clients, and dedicate yourself to delivering on the commitments you and your team make to them.\nStrong Plus\nProduction AI operations (Day 2): eval harnesses, observability and tracing, cost and token economics, drift, debugging non-deterministic systems.\nPrompt- and eval-level regression testing running in CI and gating releases.\nDelivery in regulated environments (financial services, healthcare, insurance, manufacturing).\nPre-sales support: discovery calls, SOW and estimate shaping, technical proposal defense.\nProcess mining, operations analysis, or transformation consulting background.\nClient enablement and training — building the client team’s capability, not just the system.\nPrior consulting or agency environment; comfort with ambiguity and multiple accounts.\nWork Authorization Requirements\nApplicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States. FullStack Labs is unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment visa for this position.\nFullStack Labs is an equal opportunity employer. We do not discriminate on the basis of citizenship status, immigration status, or national origin, or any other protected characteristic. FullStack Labs participates in E-Verify.\nWhat We Offer\nCompetitive Salary.\nPaid Time Off (vacation, sick leave, parental leave, holidays).\n100% remote work.\nThe ability to work with leading startups and Fortune 500 companies.\nHealth, dental, and vision insurance.\n401(k) w/ 4% match.\nAmple opportunity for career advancement.\nContinuing education opportunities.\nFullStack is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity, or Veteran status.\nLearn more about our Applicants Privacy Notice.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4486161894": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-18T01:02:47.116527+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "At Zyte, we don't just collect web data—we solve complex web data challenges at scale. We are a globally distributed team that is bold, curious, and dedicated to building innovative ways to deliver clean, reliable web data from across the internet.\nData is our passion: We unlock access to open web data, empowering organizations—from startups to global enterprises—to power competitive intelligence, analytics, and AI pipelines\nRemote-first culture: Work from anywhere in the world. With over 260 Zytans across 33 countries, our strength comes from diverse backgrounds, perspectives, and skills\nEngineering excellence: We love diving deep into complex code bases, evaluating emerging technologies, and pushing technical boundaries. If you thrive on creative problem-solving and reliably delivering production-grade solutions, you will fit right in\nEstablished system design framework: We systematically analyze functional and product requirements alongside architectural trade-offs to make informed, sustainable design decisions\nReal-world distributed systems challenges: Tackle rare engineering problems in custom networking, high-throughput streaming, and large-scale orchestration under real-world operational constraints\nStrong product ownership: Work on a profitable, market-leading platform with dedicated time and resources allocated for architectural research and strategic feature engineering\nWhy This Role?\nZyte API fetches the web through a ladder of routes: plain HTTP, headless browsers, and, for the hardest targets, Edge—our own residential network of real devices. Edge is the tier that must succeed when everything else has failed. Today, a Rust peer on residential Windows PCs long-polls a single command-and-control service (CNC) over mTLS gRPC; CNC schedules fetches onto peers, runs a CONNECT proxy gateway, owns geo-routing, per-site cooldowns, and bandwidth quotas. It must grow from thousands of nodes to tens of millions of requests a day with rock-solid reliability.\nThe Edge Platform squad owns the control plane and data plane of this residential stack across Windows, Android, and Linux. The next step is building a proper Fleet Manager: a control plane with provider adapters (volunteer PCs, mobile-IP device farms, self-hosted nodes), a reconciler, rollout control, and metrics export sitting beside CNC as the data plane. You will design and operate that system—handling the scheduling, networking, proxying, and reliability work that turns residential devices into infrastructure other squads depend on. You will work directly with the Team Lead, a Principal Engineer, and partner engineering squads across Zyte.\nWhat You'll Do\nScale the data plane. Evolve CNC from a single-replica service into a horizontally scalable fetch scheduler: node selection that respects geo, site cooldowns, jail and per-peer quotas while avoiding detectable patterns, at 50-100M requests per day\nBuild the Fleet Manager control plane. Design and ship the inventory, health, configuration and software-rollout plane for the fleet: provider adapters, a reconciler, a rollout controller and an exporter to BigQuery, so a second device provider can be onboarded without bespoke scripts\nOwn the proxy path. Operate and improve the CONNECT proxy gateway and session handling on the edge, and work with the API squad on IP reputation, proxy leases and request scheduling so Edge slots cleanly into the platform's proxy plane\nEngineer the networking. mTLS gRPC between control plane and peers, long-poll and streaming semantics over unreliable residential links, NAT and carrier-grade NAT behaviour, and bandwidth accounting that is correct under contention\nMake it reliable. Define SLOs for availability, success and latency of the Edge route; build the metrics on peer count, drop-off and bandwidth that hold us and our supply partners accountable; run blue/green rollouts of CNC and peers safely\nShare production ownership. Take part in the squad's on-call rotation, lead incident post-mortems and turn operational lessons into platform improvements\nRaise the bar. Write RFDs for scheduling, fleet management and failover; review designs across the squad; and bring distributed-systems rigour (consistency, backpressure, idempotency, blast radius) to a young codebase\nRequirements\nWho You Are\n5+ years of production Rust experience, shipping and operating services you own end to end\nDistributed systems: you have designed and run schedulers, control planes or stateful services at scale, and can reason about consistency, partitions, backpressure and idempotency without a whiteboard\nDeep networking: TCP, TLS and HTTP at the handshake and packet level, gRPC and long-lived connections across NAT and lossy links, and what a client looks like on the wire\nProxy expertise: you have built or operated forward proxies, proxy gateways or residential/ISP proxy infrastructure, and understand IP reputation, session stickiness and pool health\nOps and reliability experience: SLOs and error budgets, observability you built yourself, production incidents you led, and comfort with being on call\nCross-platform awareness: comfortable with Rust running on Windows, Linux and Android targets, and with FFI boundaries when the data plane needs them\nAsync communication: strong written communication for a globally distributed, remote-first environment\nCurious problem solver: you like finding out why a system behaves the way it does under load, and fixing the cause rather than the symptom\nOur Tech Stack\nLanguages: Rust (tokio, tonic), C++ (Cronet) at the peer boundary; Python and Java in the services we integrate with\nProtocols: gRPC and protobuf over mTLS, HTTP CONNECT proxying, the Chromium network stack and our own browserless HTTP client\nInfrastructure: GCP and Kubernetes for the control plane, Terraform, blue/green deployments; multi-cloud (OCI, GCP) and data centres (Hetzner, Servers.com) across the wider platform\nData & Messaging: Valkey, BigQuery, Confluent Kafka\nMonitoring & Observability: Prometheus, Grafana, Loki, OpenTelemetry\nBonus Points\nMobile or desktop Rust: experience shipping Rust on Android, Windows or macOS, or binding Rust to C/C++ via FFI\nFleet or device management: reconcilers, rollout controllers, IoT or volunteer-computing fleets\nAnti-bot and fingerprinting: understanding of how TLS, HTTP and IP signals are used to classify traffic\nWeb scraping & crawling experience: familiarity with the technical challenges of large-scale web data extraction\nOpen source contributions: history of contributing to Rust, networking or distributed-systems open-source projects\nWhy Join Us?\nImpact at scale: Build the residential network tier behind web-scale data pipelines for top-tier global enterprises\nAutonomy and flexibility: Enjoy a genuine remote-first culture with flexible working hours and high organizational trust\nContinuous innovation: Solve emerging, complex technical challenges as AI and web data extraction rapidly evolve\nGlobal community: Collaborate with a passionate, diverse team of distributed systems engineers and data specialists across the world\nIf you are a Rust engineer who wants to turn tens of thousands of residential devices into dependable infrastructure, we would love to hear from you. Join us in building the fleet behind web data extraction at Zyte.\nBenefits\nBy joining the Zyte team, you will:\nBecome part of a self-motivated, progressive, multi-cultural team\nHave the freedom and flexibility to work from where you do your best work\nAttend conferences and meet with team members from across the globe\nWork with cutting-edge open source technologies and tools",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4488936551": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-18T01:02:47.116527+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Company Overview\nFounded in Dubai in 2016, SQUATWOLF is a gym wear brand made for athletes who push limits, in and out of the gym. What started in the Middle East has grown into a global movement, with customers in 100+ countries. We’re on a mission to elevate the human experience through high-performance gear that drives strength, progress, and purpose.\nYour Role\nWe are looking for a motivated Mobile Application Engineer (React Native) with 1–3 years of experience to join our engineering team. The ideal candidate should have hands-on experience building, maintaining, and improving cross-platform mobile applications for Android and iOS.\nYou will work closely with senior engineers, designers, and backend developers to develop reliable, high-performance mobile applications and deliver an excellent user experience.\nWhat you will do\nDevelop and maintain cross-platform mobile applications using React Native.\nBuild reusable, scalable, and maintainable components using JavaScript or TypeScript.\nIntegrate RESTAPIs and handle asynchronous data, loading states, and error scenarios.\nImplement state management using tools such as Redux Toolkit or React Context.\nCollaborate with UI/UX designers to translate designs into responsive, pixel-perfect interfaces.\nDebug issues, fix bugs, and optimize application performance.\nWork with native Android and iOS configurations when required.\nIntegrate third-party libraries and SDKs, such as Firebase, push notifications, and analytics tools.\nParticipate in code reviews and follow coding standards and best practices.\nAssist with application testing, release builds, and publishing updates to the Google Play Store and Apple App Store.\nWork with Git and participate in Agile development processes.\nWhat we are looking for\n1–3 years of hands-on experience in React Native development.\nGood understanding of JavaScript (ES6+) and TypeScript fundamentals.\nFamiliarity with React concepts, including hooks, functional components, props, and state.\nExperience integrating REST APIs and handling JSON responses.\nUnderstanding of state management solutions such as Redux Toolkit or Context API.\nFamiliarity with navigation libraries, such as React Navigation.\nUnderstanding of mobile application layouts, responsive design, and platform-specific behavior.\nBasic knowledge of Git, debugging, and troubleshooting.\nFamiliarity with Android and iOS development environments.\nGood problem-solving skills and willingness to learn new technologies.\nAbility to work collaboratively in a team environment.\nHands-on experience using AI coding tools such as Cursor and Claude.\nNice to have\nExperience publishing applications to the Google Play Store or Apple App Store.\nFamiliarity withFirebase Analytics, Crashlytics, and push notifications.\nExperience with performance optimisation, caching, and memorymanagement.\nBasic understanding of native Android (Kotlin/Java) or iOS (Swift/Objective-C).\nExperience writing unit tests or component tests.\nWhy SQUATWOLF\nWe reward energy, ownership, and people who take initiative.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4488948133": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-18T01:02:47.116527+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Company Overview\nFounded in Dubai in 2016, SQUATWOLF is a gym wear brand made for athletes who push limits, in and out of the gym. What started in the Middle East has grown into a global movement, with customers in 100+ countries. We’re on a mission to elevate the human experience through high-performance gear that drives strength, progress, and purpose.\nYour Role\nWe are looking for a Frontend Engineer (React/ Next.js) with 1–3 years of experience to join our engineering team and help maintain and grow SQUATWOLF’s headless e-commerce store front. You will work closely with a senior engineer, designers, product and backend developers. You will ship UI features, fix bugs, keep the site fast and SEO-friendly, and look after the marketing and analytics integrations the business relies on.\nWhat you will do\nDevelop and maintain a production e-commerce storefront using React and Next.js.\nBuild reusable, maintainable components in TypeScript, styled with Tailwind CSS.\nWork with Server Components, Client Components, layouts, route handlers and Server Actions.\nChoose the right rendering and caching approach (SSR, static, ISR / revalidation, or client-side) foreach page, based on performance and SEO needs.\nIntegrate the Shopify Storefront Graph QL API (products, collections, cart) and our in-house REST API. Handle loading states, caching and errors.\nBuild and maintain a multi-store, multilingual storefront: English and Arabic (RTL), several countries and currencies, and locale-aware routing.\nTurn Figmadesigns into responsive, accessible interfaces that work in both LTR and RTL.\nImprove Core Web Vitals (LCP, INP, CLS) through image optimization, code splitting and lazy loading.\nIntegrate and maintain third-party services: tag managers and analytics (GTM, Meta, TikTok, Snapchat, Klaviyo and others), search and recommendations, reviews, loyalty, customer support chat and cross-border commerce.\nDebug issues and ensure the site works across browsers and devices, including the mobile app web view.\nVerify changes for each regional store before release and support QA and product sign-off.\nWhat we are looking for\n1–3 years of hands-on React experience, with practical Next.js experience (App Router preferred).\nGood understanding of JavaScript (ES6+) and TypeScript.\nStrong grasp of React fundamentals: hooks, functional components, props, state and component lifecycle.\nUnderstanding of Next.js routing, data fetching, Server Components vs Client Components, and rendering strategies (SSR, SSG, ISR).\nExperience consuming Graph QL APIs, as well as REST APIs and JSON responses.\nProficiency in HTML5, CSS3and responsive design, with hands-on Tailwind CSS experience.\nExperience with, or a strong interest in, internationalization (i18n), including right-to-left (Arabic) layouts.\nUnderstanding of state management with React Context or similar.\nBasic understanding of web performance and SEO principles.\nComfortable with Git, browser Dev Tools, debugging and troubleshooting.\nCareful, detail-oriented approach to changes on a live, revenue-generating site.\nGood problem-solving skills, willingness to learn, and the ability to work well in a team.\nHands-on experience using AI coding tools such as Cursorand Claude.\nNice to Have\nExperience with the Shopify Storefront API, Shopify customer accounts, or other headless commerce platforms.\nExperience with multi-region or multi-currency e-commerce.\nFamiliarity with analytics and tracking tools (Google Tag Manager, GA4, Meta Pixel / Conversions API, Klaviyo).\nExperience writing unit, component or end-to-end tests (Jest, React Testing Library, Playwright).\nWhy SQUATWOLF\nWe reward energy, ownership, and people who take initiative.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4491215043": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-18T01:02:47.116527+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About The Company\nBright Vision Technologies is a technology consulting and software development company delivering cloud, artificial intelligence, data, and enterprise solutions to organizations across the United States. The company partners with clients to address complex technology needs and build practical, dependable solutions. This position offers the opportunity to contribute to enterprise initiatives in a collaborative environment that values thoughtful engineering, teamwork, and continued professional growth.\nAbout The Role\nBright Vision Technologies is seeking a Node.js Developer for a full-time, direct W-2 position. In this role, you will design, develop, test, and support enterprise software applications and services using the technology stack selected for the project. Your work will span the software delivery lifecycle, from translating requirements into implementation through integration, release preparation, and production troubleshooting.\nThe successful candidate brings practical experience with Node.js, JavaScript or TypeScript, Express or NestJS, asynchronous programming, REST APIs, SQL or NoSQL databases, and service testing. You will work with product, architecture, quality assurance, and operations colleagues to deliver reliable, maintainable software and help improve application quality and performance.\nPosition type: Full-time, direct W-2. This opportunity is not available for C2C or 1099 arrangements. The annual salary range is $115,000–$165,000, depending on relevant qualifications and experience. Candidates with four or more years of related professional experience are encouraged to apply. U.S. citizens, Green Card holders, EAD holders, and candidates seeking an H-1B transfer are welcome to apply. Bright Vision Technologies cannot sponsor new H-1B visa petitions for this position.\nQualifications\nCandidates should have typically four or more years of experience in a related professional role, with the exact experience threshold aligned to the approved requisition. Required qualifications include professional experience building or supporting production software with Node.js and a strong working knowledge of JavaScript or TypeScript. Experience with Express or NestJS, asynchronous programming, REST APIs, SQL or NoSQL databases, and service testing is expected.\nYou should understand programming fundamentals, data structures, software design, and techniques for writing clear, maintainable code. Relevant experience with APIs, system integrations, data stores, and appropriate testing practices is important. The role also requires familiarity with Git or another source-control system, structured development workflows, and the ability to investigate defects and communicate technical findings clearly. Experience working with cross-functional teams in an Agile or iterative delivery environment is required. Experience with cloud services, automation, secure development, or applicable governance and regulatory requirements is an advantage. Relevant certifications or advanced training are also welcome.\nResponsibilities\nDesign, develop, test, and maintain application components using the project’s approved technology stack. Interpret functional and technical requirements and turn them into maintainable code, APIs, integrations, interfaces, or user-facing features. Connect applications with databases, external services, and enterprise systems using appropriate standards and practices.\nParticipate in peer code reviews, automated testing, debugging, and performance improvement. Identify and resolve software defects, contribute to release readiness, and support applications in production. Collaborate with product, architecture, quality assurance, and operations teams throughout development and delivery. Communicate progress, technical risks, and implementation decisions to relevant colleagues.\nBenefits\nThis full-time direct W-2 opportunity offers an annual salary range of $115,000–$165,000 and the chance to contribute to enterprise technology initiatives. You will work with cross-functional teams and have opportunities to develop your expertise through challenging project work and professional growth. For immediate consideration, send your resume to Hilda@bvteck.com or contact Hilda at (908) 698-4899. Learn more about Bright Vision Technologies at www.bvteck.com.\nEqual Opportunity\nBright Vision Technologies is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to providing equal employment opportunities to employees and applicants. Employment decisions are made without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, genetic information, disability, veteran status, or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, or local laws. This commitment applies to all aspects of employment, including recruitment, hiring, training, compensation, promotion, transfer, leaves of absence, termination, layoffs, and recall. Bright Vision Technologies prohibits workplace harassment and discrimination. Improper interference with an employee’s ability to perform job duties may result in disciplinary action, up to and including termination.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      }
    },
